(3) The director of the county victim-witness assistance program;
(4) A practicing attorney of the county, such attorney to be selected by the solicitor of the state court of the county;
(5) A citizen of the county, such citizen to be selected by the board of commissioners.
(b) The trustees of the board of trustees of the witness fee fund shall serve four-year terms during good behavior; provided, that the practicing attorney selected pursuant to subsection (a)(4) of this section and the citizen selected pursuant to subsection (a)(5) of this section shall serve at their pleasure during their four-year terms of office, shall not hold elective public office as a member during the term of such elective office, and the position of such member shall be deemed vacant upon such member qualifying as a candidate for elective public office. Such vacancy shall be filled for an unexpired term in the manner that original appointments are required to be made. All of such trustees shall serve without pay.
(c) The solicitor general of the state court of the county shall be the chairman of the board of trustees, and a majority of the members of such board shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of transacting all business that may come before such board. The board of trustees shall appoint a person to serve as secretary-treasurer of such board, to serve at the pleasure of the board.
